cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BreakTalk Skills: an open library of AI working instructions for Chief of Staff work, empirical research, and writing"
message: "If you use this library in work you publish, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Leiria
    given-names: Ingrid Rafaele Rodrigues
    email: "ingrid@leiriaconsulting.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6215-860X"
    affiliation: "Korea University, Sejong"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ingridleiria/breaktalk-skills"
url: "https://ingridleiria.github.io"
abstract: >-
  An open library of written working instructions, in five tracks covering
  Chief of Staff work, empirical PhD research, brand and writing, commercial and
  data analysis, and web and presentation work. Each skill states when to use it
  and when not to, the method with its decision rules, a worked example with real
  numbers, failure modes, and a checkable quality bar. The instructions are plain
  Markdown methods rather than model-specific prompts, so they can be used with
  any assistant that accepts written instructions.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - research methods
  - reproducibility
  - chief of staff
  - econometrics
  - academic writing
